---
description: NGOInfo GrantPilot build law — tiers, contracts, tests as the ruler, no fixture vocabulary. Always applies.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` before any task. It is authoritative for how work is done here.

Short form of the law:
- Contract before code; conflict → STOP and report.
- Tier the task: GREEN proceed · AMBER plan first and stop · OWNER propose only.
- `tests/contract/` is read-only for implementers. Never bend an assertion to match behaviour.
- One package, one fence. Growth → stop and say why.
- No funder name, fixture organisation, fixture phrase or expected count in prompts, engine files or engine-behaviour tests.
- Never read, print or commit secret values. `.env*` stays out of context.
- Nothing that calls a model, Railway, Stripe, storage or a production database runs without the owner's hand on the trigger.
- Claims carry pointers. Say what was not done.
